<!DOCTYPE article PUBLIC "-//NLM//DTD Journal Archiving and Interchange DTD v2.3 20070202//EN" "archivearticle.dtd"><article xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" article-type="meeting-report"><?properties open_access?><front><journal-meta><journal-id journal-id-type="nlm-ta">Br J Cancer</journal-id><journal-title>British Journal of Cancer</journal-title><issn pub-type="ppub">0007-0920</issn><issn pub-type="epub">1532-1827</issn></journal-meta><article-meta><article-id pub-id-type="pmc">1976699</article-id><article-categories><subj-group subj-group-type="heading"><subject>Meeting Report</subject></subj-group></article-categories><title-group><article-title>CRC/BACR Invited Workshop: Southampton, 29-30 September 1983 Phenotype Staging in Human Lymphoma</article-title></title-group><pub-date pub-type="ppub"><month>02</month><year>1984</year></pub-date><volume>49</volume><issue>2</issue><fpage>251</fpage><lpage>255</lpage><abstract><p>On 29 and 30 September 1983 Southampton hosted an invited Workshop sponsored jointly by the Cancer Research Campaign and the British Association for Cancer Research. Workshop Participants discussed techniques for the phenotypic analysis of human lymphoma, the relationship of these cells to normal lymphoid subpopulations and the value of this type of study in the staging of lymphoproliferative disease. The presentations reported generated extensive discussion from all participants which it is not possible to record in this brief report.</p></abstract></article-meta></front><body><supplementary-material content-type="scanned-pages"><graphic xlink:href="brjcancer00112-0125.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="251" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/><graphic xlink:href="brjcancer00112-0126.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="252" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/><graphic xlink:href="brjcancer00112-0127.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="253" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/><graphic xlink:href="brjcancer00112-0128.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="254" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/><graphic xlink:href="brjcancer00112-0129.tif" xlink:title="scanned-page" xlink:role="255" mimetype="image" mime-subtype="tiff"/></supplementary-material></body></article>